],"expires":"","revoked":false,"admin":false,"depts":["alebel-technology"],"note":"","by":"Administrator","ts":"2026-10-19T09:06:19.703Z"},"u882200abfe":{"id":"u882200abfe","email":"ajmal.ismail@alebelenergy.com","name":"Ajmal Ismail","salt":"444a0ef96b20135ddecae036b7bc5025","hash":"ea1ab8884c2189c9bde82b4f296b400db121fd7d931c3349f452065c4e93f71a","role":"ProjectManager","cats":[],"expires":"","revoked":false,"admin":false,"depts":["alebel-energy","alebel-technology"],"note":"","by":"Administrator","ts":"2026-10-19T09:16:12.753Z"},"u1f6f55ca5b":{"id":"u1f6f55ca5b","email":"ali_asif@alebel.com","name":"Ali Asif Shaikh","salt":"6486d36f78e947e5f64ab599bc5cb5be","hash":"7b858ff1c96a031a3d653c6ae3c0cf4e8b34f49dc16c1d4893510363183738c9","role":"Guest","cats":[],"expires":"","revoked":false,"admin":false,"depts":["guest"],"note":"","by":"Administrator","ts":"2026-10-19T09:41:06.656Z"}},"c":{"components":{"RJB-001":{"id":"RJB-001","cat":"Mechanical","name":"RJ ENCLOSURE","mfr":"","part":"RJ B","sup":"","fn":"Protective outer housing that contains and protects the robot's main electrical, electronic and control components.","qty":"1 set","spec":"","pur":"PENDING","asm":"NOT STARTED","rec":"PENDING","tst":"NOT TESTED","tgt":"","act":"","own":"","ov":"PENDING","issue":"Waiting for the samples","rem":"","tasks":[],"issues":[],"up":{"Purchase Status":"","Assembly Status":"","Received Status":"","Testing Status":"","Target Finish Date":"","Actual Finish Date":"","Responsible Person":"","Overall Status":""},"sec":"Mechanical Design","prio":"","start":"","desc":"","comments":[],"proj":"rjb"},"RJB-002":{"id":"RJB-002","cat":"Control / Software","name":"MAIN BOARD (STM32F407VET6)","mfr":"","part":"RJ B","sup":"","fn":"Main microcontroller (MCU) used to control and coordinate the Robot Jockey's electronic functions.","qty":"1","spec":"","pur":"ORDERED","asm":"ASSEMBLED","rec":"RECEIVED","tst":"COMPLETED","tgt":"","act":"","own":"Mohamed Mourad elsenary","ov":"REWORK","issue":"During the hardware bring-up and functional testing of the RJ Base Board, the following hardware issues and design observations were identified:\n1. CODEC Line Connectivity\nTwo CODEC devices are populated on the board, and their corresponding signal lines were found to be interconnected. This configuration may result in bus contention and unintended interaction between the two CODECs during operation.\nTo isolate the two CODECs and allow independent operation, the associated resistors R13–R18 were removed during testing. This successfully separated the relevant signal paths and prevented the two CODECs from directly interfering with each other.\n2. Missing I²C Pull-Up Resistors\nThe SCL and SDA lines of the I²C interface were found to be missing the required external pull-up resistors. Since I²C uses open-drain/open-collector signaling, appropriate pull-up resistors are required to establish the HIGH logic level on both lines.\nWithout external pull-ups, reliable I²C communication may not be possible, particularly at higher bus speeds or with increased bus capacitance.\nRecommendation: Add suitable pull-up resistors to both SCL and SDA, with the resistor value selected according to the I²C bus voltage, operating speed, and total bus capacitance.\n3. BOOT0 Configuration\nThe BOOT0 configuration requires correction. BOOT0 should be provided with a defined default logic state to ensure reliable MCU boot behavior.\nIt is recommended that BOOT0 be connected to GND through the programming/debug header. In addition, a pull-down resistor should be added to H3 pin 3 to ensure that BOOT0 remains at a defined LOW level when the header is not externally driven.\n4. Missing MIC Connection on CODEC U2\nDuring testing, it was observed that the microphone input of CODEC U2 is not connected to a microphone circuit. Hence no dedicated connector for mic connection. Floating analog audio inputs can result in unwanted noise pickup, unstable input levels, and unpredictable CODEC behavior.\nThe relevant MIC input pins of U2 were found to be floating.\n5. No Dedicated MCU SPI Interface for BLDC Motor Driver\nDuring functional interface verification, it was observed that no dedicated MCU32 pins have been allocated for SPI communication with the BLDC motor driver board.\nThe available H10 header pins could potentially be used to provide the required SPI interface; however, these pins are currently assigned to communication with the CODEC. Therefore, using H10 for the BLDC motor driver would result in a conflict with the existing CODEC interface.\nOverall Observation\nThe identified issues are primarily related to interface connectivity, default logic-state definition, missing passive components, and MCU peripheral pin allocation. These issues should be addressed at the schematic level before the next hardware revision to ensure reliable board bring-up, proper CODEC operation, stable I²C communication, predictable MCU boot behavior, and successful SPI communication with the BLDC motor driver.","rem":"Re-design the schematics & PCB","tasks":[],"issues":[],"up":{"Purchase Status":"PENDING","Assembly Status":"NOT STARTED","Received Status":"PENDING","Testing Status":"NOT TESTED","Target Finish Date":"","Actual Finish Date":"","Responsible Person":"","Overall Status":""},"sec":"Electrical / BMS Design","prio":"","start":"","desc":"","comments":[],"proj":"rjb"},"RJB-003":{"id":"RJB-003","cat":"Communication","name":"LoRa BOARD","mfr":"","part":"RJ B","sup":"","fn":"The STM32 is the main microcontroller (MCU) used to control and coordinate the Robot Jockey's electronic functions.","qty":"1","spec":"","pur":"ORDERED","asm":"ASSEMBLED","rec":"RECEIVED","tst":"COMPLETED","tgt":"","act":"","own":"Rabbia Sulaiman","ov":"REWORK","issue":"After assembly, the LoRa board was integrated with the RJ main board. When a 5V input was applied, the board was found to be shorted due to a connection through the LNA IC. The LNA connection was therefore isolated and bypassed.\nThe L2 36 nH inductor was removed and replaced with a 47 nH inductor.\nThe SKY IC got replaced for Checking PA output.\nThe R7 100 Ω resistor was removed and a connection was made from the MCU to the CTRL and DIO2 pins of the TR switch for communication.\nA second LoRa board was assembled to verify the issues observed on the first board, and the same reworks were performed on the second board.\nHowever, the PA output was still found to be low. The MCU connections to the TR switch have now been removed for further troubleshooting.\nFound the issue. The PA was not getting the correct voltage because the C8 capacitor and L2 inductor were misplaced during assembly. The C8 and L2 designators on the PCB were placed in different locations from the actual component positions, which caused the components to be assembled incorrectly.","rem":"Re-design the schematics & PCB","tasks":[],"issues":[],"up":{"Purchase Status":"PENDING","Assembly Status":"NOT STARTED","Received Status":"PENDING","Testing Status":"NOT TESTED","Target Finish Date":"","Actual Finish Date":"","Responsible Person":"","Overall Status":""},"sec":"Electrical / BMS Design","prio":"","start":"","desc":"","comments":[],"proj":"rjb"},"RJB-004":{"id":"RJB-004","cat":"Electrical / Power","name":"BLDC Motor Driver (DRV8353RS)","mfr":"","part":"RJ B","sup":"","fn":"Three-phase gate driver used to control a BLDC/PMSM motor; receives control signals from the STM32 and drives the external power MOSFETs.","qty":"1","spec":"","pur":"ORDERED","asm":"ASSEMBLED","rec":"RECEIVED","tst":"ON GOING","tgt":"","act":"","own":"Muhammad Bilal","ov":"","issue":"After completing the assembly, the board was tested and found to be heating near the 3.3V regulator when an input voltage of at least 5V was applied.\nThe 3.3V regulator and the nearby capacitors were replaced.\nAfter replacement, the issue still remained. Therefore, a second BLDC board was assembled for verification. The board was then tested section by section, and it was found that the DRV IC had an internal short.\nAfter replacing the faulty DRV IC, an output of approximately 21V was obtained. However, the DVDD pins of the DRV IC were still not receiving the required voltage, indicating another faulty DRV IC. The DRV IC was replaced again.\nAn external jumper wire was added between the SIR42 MOSFET and pin 15 of the BQ24 IC.\nAfter completing the rework, approximately 21V was obtained at all three phase output terminals of the BLDC.\nThe firmware was then flashed, and the board was tested with the BLDC motor. The motor is now operating successfully.\nDuring motor testing, an over-current condition was observed. The motor briefly drew more than the configured safety limit of 25A, causing the controller to automatically stop the motor to protect the driver, motor, and other hardware.\nTo avoid over-current during startup, the motor startup voltage/boost should be reduced, acceleration should be slowed down, and the motor should be started at a lower speed. This allows the motor more time to start without drawing excessive current. The 25A over-current safety limit should remain enabled.","rem":"Testing is on going","tasks":[],"issues":[],"up":{"Purchase Status":"PENDING","Assembly Status":"NOT STARTED","Received Status":"PENDING","Testing Status":"NOT TESTED","Target Finish Date":"","Actual Finish Date":"","Responsible Person":"","Overall Status":""},"sec":"Electrical / BMS Design","prio":"","start":"","desc":"","comments":[],"proj":"rjb"},"RJB-005":{"id":"RJB-005","cat":"Communication / RF System","name":"ANTENNA & WIRE (433MHz)","mfr":"","part":"RJ B","sup":"","fn":"Provides 433 MHz wireless communication between the Robot Jockey and the remote control/system.","qty":"1 SET","spec":"","pur":"ORDERED","asm":"ASSEMBLED","rec":"RECEIVED","tst":"NOT TESTED","tgt":"","act":"","own":"","ov":"","issue":"Waiting for TDRA Certificate","rem":"","tasks":[],"issues":[],"up":{"Purchase Status":"","Assembly Status":"","Received Status":"","Testing Status":"","Target Finish Date":"","Actual Finish Date":"","Responsible Person":"","Overall Status":""},"sec":"Electrical / BMS Design","prio":"","start":"","desc":"","comments":[],"proj":"rjb"},"RJB-006":{"id":"RJB-006","cat":"Electrical / Drive System","name":"BLDC MOTOR (BL-4820, 18-21V)","mfr":"","part":"RJ B","sup":"","fn":"Main drive motor; converts battery power into mechanical movement and controls the camel through WIPS via the motor driver.","qty":"1","spec":"","pur":"ORDERED","asm":"ASSEMBLED","rec":"RECEIVED","tst":"PASSED","tgt":"","act":"2026-10-01","own":"","ov":"COMPLETE","issue":"","rem":"","tasks":[],"issues":[],"up":{"Purchase Status":"","Assembly Status":"","Received Status":"","Testing Status":"","Target Finish Date":"","Actual Finish Date":"","Responsible Person":"","Overall Status":""},"sec":"Electrical / BMS Design","prio":"","start":"","desc":"","comments":[],"proj":"rjb"},"RJB-007":{"id":"RJB-007","cat":"Mechanical / Drive System","name":"GEARBOX (GL-PG4201401)","mfr":"","part":"RJ B","sup":"","fn":"Reduces motor speed and increases torque to provide the required driving force for the Robot Jockey and camel movement.","qty":"1","spec":"","pur":"ORDERED","asm":"ASSEMBLED","rec":"RECEIVED","tst":"PASSED WITH REMARKS","tgt":"","act":"2026-08-01","own":"","ov":"COMPLETE","issue":"","rem":"","tasks":[],"issues":[],"up":{"Purchase Status":"","Assembly Status":"","Received Status":"","Testing Status":"","Target Finish Date":"","Actual Finish Date":"","Responsible Person":"","Overall Status":""},"sec":"Mechanical Design","prio":"","start":"","desc":"","comments":[],"proj":"rjb"},"RJB-008":{"id":"RJB-008","cat":"Mechanical / Drive System","name":"GEARBOX END COVER","mfr":"","part":"RJ B","sup":"","fn":"Connects the BLDC motor to the gearbox, provides mechanical support and alignment, and protects internal gearbox components.","qty":"1","spec":"","pur":"PENDING","asm":"NOT STARTED","rec":"PENDING","tst":"NOT TESTED","tgt":"","act":"","own":"","ov":"PENDING","issue":"","rem":"","tasks":[],"issues":[],"up":{"Purchase Status":"","Assembly Status":"","Received Status":"","Testing Status":"","Target Finish Date":"","Actual Finish Date":"","Responsible Person":"","Overall Status":""},"sec":"Mechanical Design","prio":"","start":"","desc":"","comments":[],"proj":"rjb"},"RJB-009":{"id":"RJB-009","cat":"Mechanical / Drive System","name":"CONNECTING COVER (Gearbox & Motor)","mfr":"","part":"RJ B","sup":"","fn":"Connects the BLDC motor to the gearbox, ensuring alignment, secure mounting and efficient torque transfer.","qty":"1","spec":"","pur":"PENDING","asm":"NOT STARTED","rec":"PENDING","tst":"NOT TESTED","tgt":"","act":"","own":"","ov":"PENDING","issue":"","rem":"","tasks":[],"issues":[],"up":{"Purchase Status":"","Assembly Status":"","Received Status":"","Testing Status":"","Target Finish Date":"","Actual Finish Date":"","Responsible Person":"","Overall Status":""},"sec":"Mechanical Design","prio":"","start":"","desc":"","comments":[],"proj":"rjb"},"RJB-0010":{"id":"RJB-0010","cat":"Mechanical / Drive System","name":"ADATOR COUPLING (Gearbox & Whip)","mfr":"","part":"RJ B","sup":"","fn":"Connects the gearbox output to the whip mechanism for secure torque transmission and alignment for camel control.","qty":"1","spec":"","pur":"PENDING","asm":"NOT STARTED","rec":"PENDING","tst":"NOT TESTED","tgt":"","act":"","own":"","ov":"PENDING","issue":"","rem":"","tasks":[],"issues":[],"up":{"Purchase Status":"","Assembly Status":"","Received Status":"","Testing Status":"","Target Finish Date":"","Actual Finish Date":"","Responsible Person":"","Overall Status":""},"sec":"Mechanical Design","prio":"","start":"","desc":"","comments":[],"proj":"rjb"},"RJB-0011":{"id":"RJB-0011","cat":"Mechanical / Drive System","name":"WHIP","mfr":"","part":"RJ B","sup":"","fn":"","qty":"1","spec":"","pur":"PENDING","asm":"NOT STARTED","rec":"PENDING","tst":"NOT TESTED","tgt":"","act":"","own":"","ov":"PENDING","issue":"","rem":"","tasks":[],"issues":[],"